(### 2. PROBLEM STATEMENT & MOTIVATION) '
() '
(#### 2.1 Problem Statement) '
(*To design, evaluate, and implement an end-to-end intelligent grievance management ecosystem ca) '
() '
(#### 2.2 Motivation) '
(1. **Human Triage Overhead:** University administrative clerks spend hours reading complaints, ) '
(2. **Subjective Priority Assessment:** Human officers frequently underestimate the urgency of c) '
(3. **Indian English Linguistic Nuances:** Indian university students frequently blend formal bu) '
(4. **Safety & Institutional Liability:** A single delayed response to an anti-ragging complaint) '
() '
(---) '
() '
(### 3. EXISTING SYSTEM VS. PROPOSED INTELLIGRIEVANCE AI) '
() '
(| Dimension | Existing University Portals \(e.g., UGC Samadhaan / Static Forms\) | Proposed Intel) '
(|---|---|---|) '
(| **Input Ingestion** | Rigid multi-page dropdowns; students forced to select departments manua) '
(| **Categorization** | Manual selection by student \(often incorrectly routed\) | Supervised NLP ) '
(| **Priority Assignment**| Static FIFO \(First In, First Out\) or student self-selection | Superv) '
(| **Emergency Escalation**| No automated safeguard; emergency tickets wait in queue | Determini) '
(| **Duplicate Handling** | None; identical complaints flood department queues | Sublinear TF-ID) '
(| **Explainability** | Black-box / None | Feature importance attribution and key severity drive) '
(| **Hotspot Intelligence**| Manual spreadsheet generation | Automated spatial hotspot and recur) '
