() '
(#### 8.1 Sublinear TF-IDF Feature Representation) '
(For a term $t$ in document $d$ within corpus $D$, the sublinear Term Frequency-Inverse Document) '
($$\\text{TF-IDF}\(t, d, D\) = \(1 + \\ln\(\\text{TF}\(t, d\)\)\) \\cdot \\ln\\left\(\\frac{1 + |D|}{1 + |\\{d' \\) '
(Using sublinear scaling prevents repetitive words in lengthy student grievances from dominating) '
() '
(#### 8.2 Multinomial Naive Bayes Formulation) '
(Given a feature vector $\\mathbf{x} = \(x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_m\)$ representing TF-IDF values, the pr) '
($$P\(c_k \\mid \\mathbf{x}\) \\propto P\(c_k\) \\prod_{j=1}^m P\(x_j \\mid c_k\)^{x_j}$$) '
(With Laplace smoothing \($\\alpha = 0.1$\):) '
($$\\hat{\\theta}_{kj} = \\frac{N_{kj} + \\alpha}{N_k + \\alpha m}$$) '
() '
(#### 8.3 Calibrated Logistic Regression for Severity Prediction) '
(Multinomial Logistic Regression models the posterior class probabilities using the softmax func) '
($$P\(y = j \\mid \\mathbf{x}\) = \\frac{\\exp\(\\mathbf{w}_j^T \\mathbf{x} + b_j\)}{\\sum_{k=1}^K \\exp\(\\ma) '
(Class imbalance is adjusted via heuristic weighting:) '
($$w_c = \\frac{N}{K \\cdot N_c}$$) '
() '
(---) '
() '
(### 9. SEVERITY SCORING & INSTITUTIONAL SAFETY SAFEGUARDS) '
() '
(#### 9.1 Continuous Severity Formulation) '
(Rather than assigning a static categorical label, the system computes a continuous urgency scor) '
($$S\(\\mathbf{x}\) = \\sum_{p \\in \\mathcal{P}} P\(p \\mid \\mathbf{x}\) \\cdot W_p$$) '
(Where priority class weights are defined as:) '
($$\\mathcal{P} = \\{\\text{Low}: 20.0, \\text{Medium}: 45.0, \\text{High}: 75.0, \\text{Critical}: 98) '
() '
(#### 9.2 Statutory Safety Safeguard Engine) '
(To eliminate algorithmic failure on life-safety or criminal harassment complaints, a determinis) '
($$\\mathcal{R}_{\\text{hazard}} = \\text{regex}\(\\text{"ragging | assault | threat | fire | short c) '
(- If $\\mathcal{R}_{\\text{hazard}}$ evaluates to True:) '
(  $$\\text{Priority} \\leftarrow \\text{"Critical"}, \\quad S \\leftarrow \\max\(S, 94.0\), \\quad \\text) '
(- If category is `"Safety and Harassment"` and model predicts Low or Medium:) '
(  $$\\text{Priority} \\leftarrow \\text{"High"}, \\quad S \\leftarrow \\max\(S, 78.0\), \\quad \\text{SLA) '
() '
(---) '
() '
(### 10. EXPLAINABLE AI \(XAI\) & SEMANTIC DEDUPLICATION) '
() '
(#### 10.1 Feature Attribution Methodology) '
(For any predicted category $\\hat{c}$, the model decomposes the log-probability contributions of) '
($$\\phi_j\(\\mathbf{x}\) = x_j \\cdot \\log P\(x_j \\mid \\hat{c}\)$$) '
(Tokens with the largest positive contribution $\\phi_j$ are visualized in real-time on both stud) '
() '
(#### 10.2 Semantic Deduplication) '
(Incoming complaints $\\mathbf{q}$ are compared against active open cases $\\mathbf{d}_i$ in the s) '
($$\\text{Sim}\(\\mathbf{q}, \\mathbf{d}_i\) = \\frac{\\mathbf{q} \\cdot \\mathbf{d}_i}{\\|\\mathbf{q}\\|_2 ) '
ET

